# Laziness proof: $reduce accumulator not forced for an unused key.
# The callback builds a dict with both a real "sum" key and an error-trap "boom" key.
# We only access "sum" from the final accumulator. "boom" is never forced because
# dict entries are lazy thunks — the error inside "boom" never fires.
[result: [reduce
    [fn [acc x] [sum: [+ acc.sum x]  boom: [raise "accumulator key should not fire"]]]
    [sum: 0  boom: [raise "init should not fire"]]
    [10 20 30]]]
---
%.result.sum
=== out
Int(60)
